# @PROJECT@

Embedded project for **@BOARD_NAME@** (@MCU@).
Style: **bare-metal, pure register access** (no HAL).

## Layout

```
@PROJECT@/
├── src/                    application code (start here: src/main.c)
├── inc/                    headers (stm32l476_regs.h — minimal regs)
├── startup/                startup.c — vector table + reset handler
├── linker/                 linker.ld — memory map & sections
├── build/                  object files (git-ignored)
├── bin/                    .elf / .bin / .hex / .map (git-ignored)
├── .embed/                 workflow metadata (board.conf, scripts)
└── Makefile
```

## Build / flash / debug

From the project root:

| Command         | What it does                                           |
|-----------------|--------------------------------------------------------|
| `make`          | build `.elf` + `.bin` + `.hex`, print size             |
| `make flash`    | flash to the board via OpenOCD                         |
| `make erase`    | mass-erase the chip                                    |
| `make reset`    | reset the MCU                                          |
| `make openocd`  | start OpenOCD server (top debug pane)                  |
| `make debug`    | start GDB, connect, load, break at `main`              |
| `make monitor`  | open `tio` on `@SERIAL_PORT@` @ @SERIAL_BAUD@          |
| `make size`     | section size breakdown                                 |
| `make dump`     | full disassembly to `bin/*.lst`                        |
| `make ccdb`     | regenerate `compile_commands.json` (for clangd)        |
| `make clean`    | wipe `build/`, `bin/`, `compile_commands.json`         |

## tmux session layout

When launched via `embed open @PROJECT@`:

- **editor** window — nvim
- **debug** window — OpenOCD (top) + GDB (bottom), pre-typed, press Enter when ready

Popups (any window):

- `prefix + g` — shell popup
- `prefix + t` — serial monitor (tio)
- `prefix + B` — build popup
- `prefix + F` — flash popup
- `prefix + E` — erase (asks to confirm)

## Debugging workflow (typical loop)

1. Plug in the board. `lsusb` should show "STMicroelectronics ST-LINK/V2.1".
2. Go to **debug** window (`prefix + 2`).
3. Top pane: press Enter to run `make openocd`. Should print `Listening on port 3333`.
4. Bottom pane: press Enter to run `make debug`. GDB connects, loads the ELF, breaks at `main`.
5. Standard GDB: `n` / `s` / `c` / `info registers` / `x/16xw 0x48000000` etc.
6. Serial output: `prefix + t` anywhere.

## First build

```sh
make
make flash
```

LED on pin P@USER_LED_PORT@@USER_LED_PIN@ should blink.
